  "plainEnglishInsights": {
    "title": "Plain-English Summary",
    "period": "Aug 10-Aug 16, 2026",
    "updatedAt": "2026-08-17 12:30 PDT",
    "overall": "ElectricNOW still has real momentum in the broader month: rolling 28-day sessions are up, DotStudios-reported TVOD remains meaningfully elevated, Apple downloads are up versus the prior Apple snapshot, and Roku app engagement remains healthy. The one honest caveat is that the Aug. 10-Aug. 16 GA4 week eased off the prior SyFy-launch spike, so we should treat this as sustained post-spike momentum rather than another breakout week.",
    "bullets": [
      "DotStudios reports $2,231.86 in TVOD gross/net sales from 109 paid transactions for Aug 10-Aug 16. The Ark contributed $1,196.39 and The Librarians contributed $984.51, so the two campaign titles accounted for 97.7% of current TVOD sales.",
      "Purchase mix is broad: Android represented 31.0% of DotStudios TVOD revenue, web 30.9%, Apple 28.3%, Roku 9.1%, and Amazon Fire 0.7%.",
      "Apple’s latest manual App Store Connect snapshot shows 538 downloads and $673.67 gross sales for Aug 10-Aug 16; downloads are 38.7% above the prior Apple snapshot.",
      "Roku’s Aug. 17 App Engagement email shows 267 new installs, 418 average daily viewers, 76.52 average minutes per viewer, and 3,729 hours streamed for the latest Roku-side reporting window. Roku Sales Activity is also fresh for the current dashboard week and shows $197.91 gross Roku-only purchase activity.",
      "DotStudios app dashboard exports add important manual context: app installs summary shows 1476 installs and 578 updates, while the title/viewing export shows 21,555 total video views for Aug 10-Aug 16.",
      "YouTube YTD income is restored and fresh through Aug. 16 at $111,769.93. Current-period YouTube daily rows are available through Aug. 15, so Aug. 16 is treated as pending rather than zero.",
      "GA4 platform usage is softer than last week’s spike, but the rolling 28-day comparison remains positive. That means the launch surge has cooled week over week, while the larger trend still shows ElectricNOW operating above its prior baseline."
    ],
    "paidAcquisitionAssessment": {
      "verdict": "acceptable but needs proof of viewing",
      "summary": "Paid-acquisition reporting is not fully fresh this week because Google Ads is blocked by the connector’s deprecated API version and no newer Meta-only report was found. The practical read is that paid ads should keep being tested, but budget increases should be judged by install-to-viewing quality and purchase lift, not by clicks or campaign impressions alone.",
      "nextTests": [
        "Repair Google Ads API reporting or replace the connector path so first-open and cost-per-conversion values refresh again.",
        "Ask Nathan/Forge One for a Meta-only report separated from Google Ads so Meta is not double counted.",
        "Run separate The Ark and The Librarians Facebook tests in the high-purchase states, but compare downstream viewing and TVOD lift by state before scaling.",
        "Split iOS, Android, Roku, and web analysis because DotStudios purchase devices now show meaningful differences by platform.",
        "Refresh creative weekly and test show-specific urgency tied to SyFy/TNT awareness, then validate whether new installs become viewers."
      ]
    }
  },
